gpui_macos: Present the last frame when a window is shown again

macOS can discard a hidden window's contents, for example under memory
pressure. GPUI presents only after a draw or when a presentation is
required, so an idle window that is shown again, or whose layer AppKit asks
to redisplay, stays transparent until something marks it changed.

`displayLayer:` now requires a presentation, and the first display-link
frame after the window becomes visible presents the last scene, so nothing
is redrawn.

Remove when upstream gpui_macos presents again when AppKit asks for the
layer's contents.

